  "caveats": [
    "THIS PROBE CANNOT ANSWER ITS OWN QUESTION UNDER CONVENTION D. F_iso sums only l(lam) >= 3, where y_lam = 0 for all n (schurPrincipal_eq_zero_iff, wenzlLevel_conventionD). The controlled test returns the same answer for every isospin class because it returns nothing at all. The isospin question is neither answered nor refuted here — scope-(a), about this instrument.",
    "DO NOT RE-ENABLE A CROSSING SCAN ON THIS OBJECT. The residual is round-off, it is (Z,N)-dependent because the braid word is by design the only varying input, and its ordering is not stable in q. A bisect-on-sign-change produces isospin-correlated crossings that are artifact, and the previous verdict logic would have reported them as a surviving pattern.",
    "pp(2,0), nn(0,2), 4Li(3,1), 4H(1,3) are COMBINATORIAL PROBES of the braid word, NOT bound nuclides — the diproton/dineutron are unbound and 4H/4Li are unbound resonances. They are used only because atom_braid_word_3A(Z,N) is defined for any (Z,N). No physical prediction is made about them and AME is never consulted.",
    "THE CONFOUND AND THE COST LAW ARE CONVENTION-INDEPENDENT AND SURVIVE. In {D,T,3He,4He,6Li,7Li} isospin and strand count move together (Z=N <=> A even), so the A-ladder cannot separate them however many isotopes are added; and Sum_lam dim^2 = n! puts 6Li/7Li out of reach by orders of magnitude. Both stand whatever happens to the sign question."
  ],
